# ✅ **4) Relational Operator Overloading ( < )**

## 🎯 What it does  
Compare distances:

```
if (D1 < D2)
```

Compare feet → if equal compare inches.

---

## ⭐ **Simple Code ( < Overload )**

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class Distance {
    int feet, inches;

public:
    Distance(int f = 0, int i = 0) {
        feet = f;
        inches = i;
    }

    // Overload <
    bool operator<(Distance d) {
        if (feet < d.feet)
            return true;

        if (feet == d.feet && inches < d.inches)
            return true;

        return false;
    }

    void show() {
        cout << feet << " feet " << inches << " inches\n";
    }
};

int main() {
    Distance D1(11, 10);
    Distance D2(15, 11);

    if (D1 < D2)
        cout << "D1 is less than D2\n";
    else
        cout << "D2 is less than D1\n";

    return 0;
}
```

✔ Output: `D1 is less than D2`

