# 🚀 PART 2 — POINTERS TO OBJECTS

## ⭐ What is a pointer to an object?

Just like:

```
int *p;
```

you can create:

```
item *ptr;
```

This pointer can store the address of an object.

---

## ⭐ Simple Example

```cpp
item x;
item *ptr = &x;
```

Now you can access members in 2 ways:

### ✔ 1) Using dot (.) operator  
```cpp
x.getdata(100, 75.5);
x.show();
```

### ✔ 2) Using arrow ( → ) operator  
```cpp
ptr->getdata(100, 75.5);
ptr->show();
```

Both are SAME.

---

# 🎯 CLEAN C++ CODE FOR POINTERS TO OBJECTS

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class item {
    int code;
    float price;

public:
