# 📌 6) Rules for Virtual Functions (Exam important)

1. Must be member of a class  
2. Cannot be static  
3. Accessed using a base pointer  
4. Base class version must be defined (even if empty)  
5. Derived versions must have SAME signature  
6. Used for runtime binding  
7. Virtual constructors NOT allowed  
8. Virtual destructors allowed  
9. If defined only in base → base version called  
10. If not redefined in derived, base version runs

