# ⭐ 1) **Single Inheritance**
**Definition:**  
One base class → one derived class.

```
A → B
```

### ✔ SIMPLE EXAMPLE

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class A {
public:
    void showA() {
        cout << "This is class A\n";
    }
};

class B : public A {   // single inheritance
public:
    void showB() {
        cout << "This is class B\n";
    }
};

int main() {
    B obj;
    obj.showA();   // from A
    obj.showB();   // from B
}
```

---

# ⭐ 2) **Multilevel Inheritance**
**Definition:**  
One derived becomes base for another derived.

```
A → B → C
```

### ✔ SIMPLE EXAMPLE

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class A {
public:
    void showA() {
        cout << "Class A\n";
    }
};

class B : public A {   // A → B
public:
    void showB() {
        cout << "Class B\n";
    }
};

class C : public B {   // B → C
public:
    void showC() {
        cout << "Class C\n";
    }
};

int main() {
    C obj;
    obj.showA();
    obj.showB();
    obj.showC();
}
```

---

# ⭐ 3) **Multiple Inheritance**
**Definition:**  
One class inherits from **two or more** base classes.

```
A →  
      \
       C
      /
B →
```

### ✔ SIMPLE EXAMPLE

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class A {
public:
    void showA() {
        cout << "Class A\n";
    }
};

class B {
public:
    void showB() {
        cout << "Class B\n";
    }
};

class C : public A, public B {  // multiple inheritance
public:
    void showC() {
        cout << "Class C\n";
    }
};

int main() {
    C obj;
    obj.showA();
    obj.showB();
    obj.showC();
}
```

